---
name: Map an OpenSSH message to OCSF
description: |
  Normalizes one `sshd` message body to OCSF Authentication. The normalizer
  parses the message, takes the timestamp and host from the Syslog envelope,
  maps the structured event, and preserves the body as OCSF provenance.
---

from {
  timestamp: 2026-01-01T00:00:00Z,
  hostname: "bastion-01",
  message: "Failed password for invalid user admin from 198.51.100.42 port 49152 ssh2",
}
openssh::ocsf::normalize message, time=timestamp, hostname=hostname
ocsf::derive
